Doubly Linked List Implementation

This C++ program implements a menu-driven Doubly Linked List using a 0-based index system. Each node holds an integer data value, a pointer to the previous node, and a pointer to the next node.

Operations Included
Insert at Position inserts a new element at a given 0-based index. If the position is out of bounds, it displays an error message.
Delete at Position removes the node at a given 0-based index and returns the deleted value.
Search traverses the list to find the first occurrence of a given element and prints its 0-based index.
Display prints all elements currently in the list from head to tail.

Time Complexity
Insert at Position: O(1) at the head (position 0), O(n) for arbitrary positions in the worst case.
Delete at Position: O(1) at the head (position 0), O(n) for arbitrary positions in the worst case.
Search: O(n) in the worst case.
Display: O(n) to traverse all nodes.
Space Complexity: O(n) to store n nodes, with O(1) auxiliary space per operation.

